@startuml
title doctor-cam - High-Level Architecture
!pragma layout elk
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 600
skinparam dpi 180
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Android App" {
  [MainActivity / Fragments] as UI
  [Camera Module] as Camera
  [Preview Surface] as Preview
  [PaddleDetectionFragment] as PaddleFrag
  [Utils (Java)] as Utils
  [Assets (model.nb, labels, configs)] as Assets
  [Storage / Cache] as Cache
}

package "Native Layer (JNI / C++)" {
  [Native Bridge (JNI)] as JNI
  [Pipeline (C++)] as Pipeline
  [Detector (C++ abstraction)] as Detector
  [PaddleLite Runtime] as PaddleLite
  [OpenCV (native libs)] as OpenCV
}

package "Model & Data" {
  [Detection Model (.nb)] as ModelFile
  [Label List] as Labels
  [Pre/Post-process Params] as Params
}

UI --> PaddleFrag : user interaction / open camera
Camera --> Preview : camera frames (YUV/RGBA)
Preview --> PaddleFrag : frame callback (Bitmap/Mat)
PaddleFrag --> Utils : copy model to cache on startup
Assets --> Utils : read model/labels from assets
Utils --> Cache : write model.nb and label.txt

PaddleFrag --> JNI : call native Process(Mat/byte[])
JNI --> Pipeline : forward to Pipeline::Process
Pipeline --> Detector : call detector_->Process(...)
Detector --> PaddleLite : build input tensor and run inference
Detector --> OpenCV : resize, normalize, NMS, visualize
PaddleLite --> ModelFile : load model.nb
Detector --> Labels : read class mapping
Pipeline --> JNI : return detections (boxes, scores, classes)
JNI --> PaddleFrag : callback with results
PaddleFrag --> UI : draw boxes/labels on Preview

note right of Detector
  Detector internals:
  - Preprocess (resize, normalize, transpose)
  - Inference (PaddleLite)
  - Postprocess (NMS, threshold)
  - Output conversion (object list)
end note

note left of OpenCV
  OpenCV provides:
  - Mat operations
  - Image visualization (boxes/text)
  - Optional DNN APIs as fallback
end note

database "Optional" {
  [Saved Images / Logs]
}
PaddleFrag --> "Saved Images / Logs" : optionally save detection results

@enduml